# How to Design Data (HTDD)

## 1. Data Definition

A Wrestler is a compound data structure made up of the following fields:

| Field | Type |
| ----- | ---- |
| name  | String |
| height | Float |
| weight | Float |
| wrestler-type | List of strings (primary and secondary) (well-balanced, brawler, grappler, mat technician, high flyer, rule breaker). Wrestler type will determine moveset. |
| moveset | List of Strings. Wrestler's signature moves (finisher included)
| static-stats | Dictionary of String : Float (keys: strength, speed, durability, counter, charisma, submission, aerial ability) |
| dynamic-stats | Dictionary (see below for breakdown) |

### wrestler-type breakdown:

| Field | Description |
| ----- | ---- |
| well-balanced | Does not rely on single dominant techniques. Well-balanced wrestlers are effective in all ways of fighting. Does not have any affect on stats | 
| brawler | Relies on hard hits, strength and brute force. Brawlers typically have high durability and strength, but low aerial ability and submission stats. |
| grappler | Coming soon...

### moveset breakdown:

| Field | Type |
| ----- | ---- |
| well-balanced | list of strings |
etc


### static-stats description:

| Field | Type |
| ----- | ---- |
| Strength | Wrestler's power. Wrestlers with high strength are more effective against wrestler's with low strength. Wrestlers with high strength often struggle against wrestlers with high counter, speed, and submission. |

### dynamic-stats breakdown:

| Field | Type |
| ----- | ---- |
| Health | Float |
| Fatigue | Float |
| Morale | String: confident, nervous, rattled, furious, demoralized |
| Momentum | Boolean |
| Archetype | String: heel, tweener, babyface |
| injury status | Dictionary of String: String - see breakdown below |